er  2072 metres long  to see why this is the problem let's  analyze runway length requirements basic  runway length is determined by airplane  performance and to calculate it we need  to analyze the critical moments in an  aeroplanes take-off sequence the plane  hits six critical speeds during takeoff  the first is the stall speed this is the  minimum speed at which a plane will  remain airborne this is not used as a  take-off speed as any decrease in speed  due to fluctuations and wind or  orientation of the plane will cause the  plane to fall the next critical speed is  the minimum control speed this applies  to multi-engine aircraft only if a  multi-engine aircraft loses an engine  the uneven thrust between the wings will  cause the plane to turn this is called  yaw in aviation to counteract this the  rudder will be deflected to provide the  opposite yawing moment the rudder needs  air passing over it to work and thus the  minimum control velocity is the velocity  at which the rudder can provide enough  of a yaw moment to keep the plane  straight in the event of an engine  failure the next be the pilot needs to  worry about is v1 v1 is a line in the  sand for pilots making decisions whether  to abort a takeoff if something happens  before v1 like an engine failure the  pilot must abort the takeoff if it  happens above the 1 they must continue  with the take-off as it would be unsafe  to stop this is the most important speed  for a runway designers at this speed the  plane will need enough distance  on the runway to safely bring the plane  to a stop which is exactly the same as  the distance needed to reach v1 the  resulting total runway length is dust  called the balanced field leant back to  that in a moment  the fourth critical speed is VR or the  rotation speed this is the point the  plane can begin to lift its nose and  begin its ascent the next beam which  results some of the coolest testing  videos is the minimum on stick speed  this is the speed the plane 